// b.sx authors its OWN `apply` taking a POINTER. `from_b` passes a value local
// `v` bare; the pointer param drives implicit address-of so the callee mutates
// `v` in place (×2 → 42), typed against this author rather than a.sx's
// value-param winner.
apply  :: (x: *i64) { x.* = x.* * 2; }
from_b :: () -> i64 { v : i64 = 21; apply(v); return v; }
